{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4ff","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0cf67-8ef1-7242-9863-cfd3eed876a3"},"sequence":218,"recorded_at":1780531400000431,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"697f866a-e541-452f-adbf-d5da32c23417","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"697f866a-e541-452f-adbf-d5da32c23417","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"697f866a-e541-452f-adbf-d5da32c23417"},"call_id":"call_01a0cf6843a67157a907895496e043f5","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-9-1\",\n  \"command\": \"/Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-2ya5le) { full }' 2>&1 | python3 -m json.tool 2>&1 | head -n 400\",\n  \"description\": \"Get full task element\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\n    \\\"ac\\\": \\\"Production behavior demonstrates: Implement exact/semantic/summarized/opaque_preserved/synthesized/omitted/unrecoverable dispositions and stable reason codes. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\\\",\\n    \\\"assignee\\\": \\\"[implementer] developer (muse)\\\",\\n    \\\"blockedBy\\\": [\\n        \\\"TASK-260830-32ypr2\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"blocks\\\": [\\n        \\\"TASK-260830-1jmmqn\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"checklist\\\": [\\n        {\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Implement exact/semantic/summarized/opaque_preserved/synthesized/omitted/unrecoverable dispositions and stable reason codes\\\",\\n            \\\"done\\\": true\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\n            \\\"done\\\": true\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\n            \\\"done\\\": true\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"Closed vocabularies by exhaustive enumeration against an independent oracle written from pinned SPEC v0.7.0 \\\\u00a713.14.2 (10548+): the seven dispositions, the five profiles, the strategies, and every closed core reason code are admitted exactly; every other token (case variants, whitespace, near-misses, empty, non-string) is refused with a literal code; a reverse-DNS extension reason is admitted but can never redefine or shadow a core code; each has a narrowing its named test kills when run alone\\\",\\n            \\\"done\\\": true\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"FidelityDispositionRecord rules pinned over the full (disposition x reason-set-cardinality x canonical_object_id presence x source-evidence presence) grid: exact requires an empty reason set, every other disposition at least one reason, synthesized requires no source canonical object, every non-synthesized row traces to captured source evidence; field bounds (string lengths, sorted-unique arrays) refused at edge and edge+1\\\",\\n            \\\"done\\\": true\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"Fidelity Report 1.0.0 closed schema: exact member set, fidelity_report_id as the JCS digest with only that member omitted (independently recomputed in the test), archive vs target branch-exact nullability, dispositions sorted unique by source item key with synthesized rows after source rows, counts/event_kind_counts/content_block_counts/byte_counts/reason_counts derived from the rows and reconciled exactly; a report whose aggregates disagree with its rows is refused\\\",\\n            \\\"done\\\": true\\n        },\\n        {\\n            \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gate x entry census with the domain axes above in the conformance matrix and TRACEABILITY, isolated kill attribution, importer outcome grid keyed (package