ecode with the\n25|  four record rules (exact⟺empty reasons; non-exact≥1;\n26|  synthesized⇒null canonical; evidence presence for all rows).\n27|- `report.go` — `BuildFidelityReport` / `DecodeFidelityReport` for\n28|  the closed 29-member Fidelity Report 1.0.0: branch-exact\n29|  archive/target nullability, row ordering (source sorted, then\n30|  synthesized sorted, keys unique), derived counts/reason counts,\n31|  closed 26-kind / 8-type breakdowns reconciled per disposition,\n32|  closed 7-key byte map, policy map, and omit-self identity.\n33|- `decode.go`, `errors.go`, `doc.go` — delegated parse helpers,\n34|  `ErrInvalid` refusal identity, authority/reuse/bounds doc.\n35|\n36|Landed-owner touch (reviewed diff: +67/−1, purely additive):\n37|\n38|- `internal/clonebundle`: `CheckExtensionsClosed`,\n39|  `EncodeExtensions`, `OmitSelfDigest`, `EventKinds`,\n40|  `ContentBlockTypes`, `ValidContentBlockType` — one-line delegates\n41|  over tested internals.\n42|- `internal/environ`: `CheckReverseDNS` (new) + `CheckExtensions`\n43|  refactored onto it (one line, behavior-identical).\n44|\n45|Nothing else changed. No README/doctor/config surface (a library,\n46|not a command); no registry edit; no sibling contract.\n47|\n48|## AC coverage: 40 of 40 rows driven and measured\n49|\n50|`TASK-260830-2ya5le_conformance-matrix.md` (attached): 40 AC rows,\n51|each driven through a production entry by a named committed test;\n52|every gate row carries a directly-reddening narrowing (§A). The\n53|35-test suite (333 pass lines incl. subtests) is green with 97.1%\n54|statement coverage. Honest accounting: row 24 carries the\n55|byte-reconciliation stated bound (rows carry no byte measure, so no\n56|row reconciliation is expressible — keys + uint53 gated, bound\n57|proven by admission); rows 33–36 are admitted properties /\n58|cross-checks with no gate to narrow (disclosed, not waived).\n59|\n60|Key enumerations (oracles retyped from spec text, never imported):\n61|\n62|- Vocabularies: 7 + 5 + 5 + 19 members admitted; 24 + 17 + 15 + 27\n63|  refusal tokens plus empty plus 5 non-strings each refused with\n64|  literal codes; core/extension disjointness asserted per core code.\n65|- Record grid: 7 × {0,1,2,128,129} × canonical × evidence = 140\n66|  cells through both entries (35 admit / 105 refuse, first-fire\n67|  literals asserted).\n68|- Aggregates: counts 14-cell ±1 sweep; reason 6-cell sweep +\n69|  extra/missing/zero keys; event-kind 182-cell +1 sweep + 7 −1;\n70|  content-block 56-cell +1 + 7 −1; byte keys/values + 6 bad shapes.\n71|- Identity: test-side JCS recompute agrees; omitting any other\n72|  member disagrees; zero/flipped/non-digest claims refuse.\n73|- Member sets: 29 + 11 + 7 unknown + every-missing sweeps.\n74|- Bounds: 5 string bounds × edge/edge+1 × 2 entries + 512/513\n75|  multibyte; evidence 65536/65537 ×3 arrays; attestations 64/65;\n76|  forbid 128/129; rows 0/1/1000001 at entries + 999999/1000000 at\n77|  the factored gate.\n78|\n79|## Mutants\n80|\n81|`internal/clonefidelity/testdata/mutant_harness.py`: 62 narrowing\n82|rows + harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED control. Battery executed\n83|TWICE on the final tree, exit 0, 63/63 `ok:` lines each run (62\n84|KILLED + control SURVIVED), one raw log per plant per run\n85|(`mutants/run1/`, `mutants/run2/` in the archive). Shared gates\n86|carry one plant with a dual-entry killer; twice-implemented rules\n87|carry one plant per side. `N-disposition-route` and\n88|`N-reason-core-route` are the token-preserving attacks, killed by\n89|the behavioral oracle suites. `N-record-synth-canonical` is\n90|labelled single-member class. Zero gate survivors: the only\n91|SURVIVED verdict is the control, whose survival states that the\n92|harness observes outcomes instead of hard-coding kills.\n93|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` (verified).\n94|\n95|## Validation reran (this run, final tree)\n96|\n97|All 30 configured commands from `task-board.config.json`\n98|(`spa