{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cbbd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0cf67-8ef1-7242-9863-cfd3eed876a3"},"sequence":1081,"recorded_at":1780531400002157,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"697f866a-e541-452f-adbf-d5da32c23417","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"697f866a-e541-452f-adbf-d5da32c23417","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"697f866a-e541-452f-adbf-d5da32c23417"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0cf71-1b76-7af0-9f7e-7a68ddd4a570"},"task_id":"01a0cf71-1b76-7af0-9f7e-7a68ddd4a570","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0cf71-1b76-7af0-9f7e-7a68ddd4a570","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-7\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# TASK-260830-2ya5le Results — implement-fidelity-report-and-reason-registry\n-\n-Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n-worktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-21bxa3`, tip `0ca3e4c`);\n-no commit on the Story branch. This is the FIRST leaf of\n-STORY-260830-21bxa3; the Change Request is `task_delta` (no\n-registry edit — the Story's final leaf carries it).\n+# TASK-260830-2ya5le Results — implement-fidelity-report-and-reason-registry (rev2 rework)\n+\n+Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n+worktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-21bxa3`, tip `0ca3e4c`);\n+no commit on the Story branch. This is the FIRST leaf of\n+STORY-260830-21bxa3; the Change Request is `task_delta` (no\n+registry edit — the Story's final leaf carries it).\n+\n+Rev2 answers review verdict rev1 (`unbound-byte-aggregate`,\n+CHANGES REQUESTED) per the orchestrator rework decision: pinned\n+SPEC v0.7.0 §13.14.2 lists `byte_counts` as a \"closed map of every\n+disposition to uint53\" that must \"reconcile exactly to the rows\"\n+(lines 10636/10645), but `FidelityDispositionRecord` carries no\n+byte measure — the only byte measure in §13.14 is\n+`CaptureItem.byte_count` in §13.14.1 (line 10471), on the Capture\n+Manifest, and the spec defines no byte basis for canonical-event\n+or synthesized rows. That is a gap in the specification, not a\n+defect closable by inference, and guessing bytes from digests or\n+row counts is forbidden. Decision: `byte_counts` is\n+shape-validated in this leaf and carried as an explicit STATED\n+BOUND. \"The DoD item on aggregates is satisfied by the decision\n+above.\" Rev2 delta vs rev1 is exactly three non-production files\n+(verified byte-identical production via the rev1 CR patch: all 10\n+production files identical): the `TestByteCounts` rename into an\n+explicit bound witness, two harness killer-name strings, and two\n+TRACEABILITY rows. Zero production bytes changed.\n","final_result":true}}}
